      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The island’s first major settlement, Utsalady, grew around sawmills that processed timber from the surrounding forests.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camano_Island",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kikiallus Coast Salish people kept winter villages at Utsalady and Madrona, while Snohomish tribes camped south of Point Demock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historylink.org/File/22578",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historically, ferries linked Camano Island to Coupeville and Everett, but those routes are no longer active.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camano_Island",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A permanent library opened in August 2015 at Terry’s Corner after voters approved a $2.3 million bond to remodel a former restaurant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
